RUBRIC:{"title":"Ethics Report Rubric","total":null,"criteria":[{"id":"C1","name":"Introduction — Identifies ethical issues and broad links to engineering design; discusses the context of ethical issues in engineering organisations; identifies relevant stakeholders when considering the ethical issues.","weight":20,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":10,"max":10,"desc":"Several ethical issues and their significance identified, described, in the context of engineering design, understanding of BOTH context in engineering organisations and stakeholder interest is demonstrated."},{"label":"Very good","min":8,"max":8,"desc":"Several ethical issues identified, described, and linked to engineering design, understanding of context in engineering organisations OR stakeholder interest is demonstrated."},{"label":"Good","min":6,"max":6,"desc":"Few ethical issues identified, described, and linked to engineering design, but understanding of context and stakeholders is limited."},{"label":"Satisfactory","min":4,"max":4,"desc":"Few ethical issues identified and described, but the context and stakeholders are not identified."},{"label":"None","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"No ethical issues identified."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Balanced Discussion — Discusses objective arguments for and against decisions on the ethical issues; draws a conclusion on how stakeholders should make decisions about the issues.","weight":20,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":10,"max":10,"desc":"Objective arguments are made with significant depth, leading to conclusions on decision making recommendations for several different stakeholders."},{"label":"Very good","min":8,"max":8,"desc":"Objective arguments are made with appropriate depth. Conclusions are made on decision making, though lack of consideration of different stakeholders."},{"label":"Good","min":6,"max":6,"desc":"Arguments are made, though they lack depth or are based on personal opinion. Conclusions are made on decision making, though lack of consideration of different stakeholders."},{"label":"Satisfactory","min":4,"max":4,"desc":"Ideas are presented, though they lack the depth required to build arguments. Conclusion is made with no apparent link to the arguments."},{"label":"None","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"No arguments presented. No conclusions drawn."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Compelling Argument that supports conclusion — The report forms a compelling argument that justifies the conclusion; the body follows a logical structure, with linked paragraphs and content ordered to support the argument; arguments demonstrate a systematic understanding of the ethical issues for all stakeholders.","weight":20,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":10,"max":10,"desc":"Arguments are compelling, supported by the report structure. The conclusion is well supported by the arguments. The arguments demonstrate a systematic understanding of the ethical issues for all stakeholders."},{"label":"Very good","min":8,"max":8,"desc":"Arguments are compelling, supported by the report structure. The arguments support the conclusion, demonstrating a sound understanding of ethical issues."},{"label":"Good","min":6,"max":6,"desc":"Arguments are logically structured, though are not compelling. Conclusion is not well supported by the arguments presented."},{"label":"Satisfactory","min":4,"max":4,"desc":"Arguments are difficult to follow. Link to conclusion is unclear."},{"label":"None","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Arguments are not evident. No conclusions drawn."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Research and Evidence — Arguments are substantiated with adequate references and qualitative/quantitative evidence; research demonstrates a balanced, in-depth understanding of the topic.","weight":20,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":10,"max":10,"desc":"Arguments are well substantiated with references as well as both qualitative and quantitative evidence. Evidence of research demonstrates a balanced and in-depth understanding of the topic and its ethical issues."},{"label":"Very good","min":8,"max":8,"desc":"Arguments are substantiated with adequate references and some qualitative/quantitative evidence. Research demonstrates a good understanding of the topic."},{"label":"Good","min":6,"max":6,"desc":"Arguments are substantiated with some relevant references and qualitative OR quantitative evidence. Research demonstrates a moderate understanding of the topic."},{"label":"Satisfactory","min":4,"max":4,"desc":"Limited references that lack relevance to arguments, showing limited evidence of research."},{"label":"None","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"No references, or other evidence of research to support arguments."}]},{"id":"C5","name":"Report Structure, Format and Language — The report includes appropriate sections serving their functions (abstract, introduction, body, and conclusion); maps, figures, tables, and visual elements are correctly used to support discussion; writing is grammatically correct, fluent, concise, easy to read and understand, and uses appropriate word choice; references are well-structured and appropriate, supporting the report’s motivations.","weight":20,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":10,"max":10,"desc":"The report is fluently written, has no incorrect uses of language, uses several types of visual elements competently, and uses relevant references extensively."},{"label":"Very good","min":8,"max":8,"desc":"The report is fluently written, has no incorrect uses of language, uses several types of visual elements competently, and uses relevant references."},{"label":"Good","min":6,"max":6,"desc":"The report is fluently written, has no incorrect uses of language, uses limited visual elements, and a few relevant references."},{"label":"Satisfactory","min":4,"max":4,"desc":"The report is fluently written, has few incorrect uses of language, very limited visual elements, and few, mostly irrelevant references."},{"label":"None","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"The report has incorrect uses of language, has no visual elements, expression is not fluent, and references are missing."}]}],"notes":""}
TASK:{"title":"To Ship or Not to Ship: Engineering Ethics Case Report","overview":"Write an individual report analysing the ethical decisions stakeholders face in Rachel’s quality-assurance scenario. Evaluate whether shipping servers with known defects is ethical, explain how to decide whether to ship, and recommend what Rachel should do. Support all arguments with reputable evidence, including external case studies, and consider the consequences for all affected stakeholders.","deliverables":["A written report with an approximately 150-word abstract, introduction, body and conclusion.","A justified recommendation for Rachel on whether and under what conditions the servers should be shipped."],"format":{"length":"Maximum 1,500 words for the introduction, body and conclusion combined; abstract is approximately 150 words and excluded from the limit. References and figures are also excluded.","structure":"Include an abstract, introduction, body and conclusion. Body headings are optional; the body may be organised freely.","other":"Figures and tables are permitted. Use a consistent, established referencing style, such as Harvard or IEEE."},"requirements":[{"id":"R1","text":"Analyse the scenario in which Rachel, a quality-assurance engineer, has limited time to test servers and must decide whether to ship products with known defects. Address the distinction between possible physical harm and a higher likelihood of failure causing customer data loss."},{"id":"R2","text":"Discuss whether this is an ethical way to conduct business and how Rachel should determine when a product with known defects may be shipped."},{"id":"R3","text":"Evaluate the decision trade-offs, including the time and testing constraints, competitive pressure, company revenue and growth, Rachel’s employment interests, and the potential for large-scale testing to inform future safety improvements."},{"id":"R4","text":"Address the government health department contract and the potential for server failure to cause improper health administration or catastrophic consequences for hospitals, emergency services, and the business."},{"id":"R5","text":"Identify and discuss relevant ethical issues and stakeholder perspectives, considering arguments and consequences both for and against possible decisions."},{"id":"R6","text":"Research the ethical considerations thoroughly and support all arguments with reputable evidence and external case studies. A conclusion based only on compliance with law or regulation is insufficient."},{"id":"R7","text":"Conclude with a holistic, evidence-based and justified recommended course of action for Rachel."}]}
